<title>USA: Kellogg says Grain Millers contract ratified.</title>
<headline>Kellogg says Grain Millers contract ratified.</headline>
<dateline>BATTLE CREEK, Mich. 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kellogg Co and the American Federation of Grain Millers said on Monday a new three-year master contract between them was ratified by a 52 to 48 percent margin.</p>
<p>The agreement covers employees represented by the AFGM at Kellogg cereal plants in Battle Creek, Mich.; Omaha, Neb.; Lancaster, Pa.; and Memphis, Tenn., they said.</p>
<p>The contract includes continuation of a cost of living allowance provision, an estimated wage increase of $1.43 per hour over the agreement's term, pension increases and improved life and health insurance benefits, they said.</p>
<p>--Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787</p>
</text>
